  "description": "Works to tree with a TCA: T1 - Hawthorn Tree - growing in the front garden\rTo crown thin by 20%, removing vertical water shoots and to allow more dappled light through into the front garden.\rTo cut back to clear obstruction to the street tree, to suitable growing points, from a current branch length of 4m, reducing by 1m, to a finished length of 3m. \rTo lift to give a 6m ground clearance over the road.\rTo lift to give a 2m ground clearance over the public footpath.\rTo cut back to clear obstruction to the property, to suitable growing points, to give a 2m clearance; from a current branch length of 4m, reducing by 1m, to a finished branch length of 3m. \r\rT2 - Moribund Pear Tree - growing in the rear garden, on the left-hand side. \rThis tree is in decline, it has cavities in the main trunk and the bark on the trunk is falling off. \rTo fell to as low as possible above existing ground level.",
